  "interpretation": "The arch is a shallow moulding on an opaque west wall. North of it a separately glazed casement has a green sheet hood. In the current photograph the horizontal red band below the arch terminates before that opening. In the 2015 photograph the matching visible line is slender and muted.",
  "limits": "Photo measurement uncertainties about 0.20 m horizontally, 0.20 m vertically and 0.03–0.06 m on relief depth. The streetward arch spring is covered by a pole in 2021 and is reconstructed by symmetry. The 2018 Commons photograph faces the southern elevation; 2015 and 2021 west views establish the same side feature on both sides of the 2018 date.",
  "front_comparison": {
    "2018": "The fixed, broad, light-coloured arched wall surround exists behind the separate blue-green horizontal canopy in the 2018 street photograph.",
    "2025": "Figure 37 shows multiple fine parallel light ribs running across the dark underside of the burgundy canopy, converging toward the hanging points. These are the frame of the projecting canopy. The photograph does not isolate a second later full-width masonry arch behind the fabric."
